      <DT><font color="#00FF00" size="3"><b>WW adventures</b></font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><br>Posted on 6/7/01 02:58 AM by </font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><b>Tuene</b></font>
      <DD><font color="#FFFFCC"
size="2">Dragon spanking time, short stroll through a bunch of dragons in WW, gathering some info, farming some talismans, drinking a Bud, and getting a fair amount of head(s).<br><br>Random do-dads that were collected (this is by no means a complete list... missing dragon armor pieces to guild bank, and head turn in item distribution to be determined later):<br><br>Stronghorn's horn: Scor<br>Mazi Talisman: Cheflatho<br>Worked dragon legs: Daeeron<br>Jen Separa Talisman: Greymar<br>Worked dragon legs: Relm<br>Pantrilla's Talisman: Amlurial<br>Mazi Talisman: Qyen<br>Vitaela Talisman: Tuene<br>Vraptin Talisman: Thrudd<br>Von's Talisman: Damoiny<br>Worked dragonwing cloak: Tura<br>Harla Dar's Talisman: Sashinal<br>Tsiraka's Claws: Daeeron<br>Shardwing Courier KD quest item: Banton<br>Vraptin's Talisman: Banton<br>Neordla's Talisman: Megatryphe<br>Dragonwing (+9 wis I believe) Cloak: Shalian<br>Von's Talisman: Elesa<br>Stronghorn's horn: Thrudd<br><br>Good time, decent turnout, and the always amusing addiction of killing dragons.  Thanks to those who came out to play tonight,<br><br>Tuene<br><br></font><br><p align="center"><img src="http://www.dealersofdeath.com/images/divider.gif" width="380" height="36"></p><br><br>
    
      <DT><font color="#00FF00" size="3"><b>Quick ToV jaunt</b></font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><br>Posted on 6/6/01 07:32 PM by </font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><b>Tuene</b></font>
      <DD><font color="#FFFFCC"
size="2">Small hop into ToV, through the drop down and no further last night... few odds and ends dropped and the only thing abnormal was the heralding of the next apocalypse, as Kalourde finally was badgered into looting a piece (bout time!).  Also once again, we showed that indeed VI loves Woodelf Druids best, after seeing the green paper towel which passes for NW legs on a hobbit... lamenting my drunken choice of a first char, again.  Here's the trinkets in lazy format:<br><br>leather bracer - Tuene<br>plate bracer - Harkaelian<br>silk legs - Deception<br>plate bracer - Qyen<br>leather legs - Tuene<br>chain boots - Kalourde<br>plate bracer - Tura<br>plate gloves - Astur<br>leather boots - Ranodill<br>plate gloves - Chold<br><br></font><br><p align="center"><img src="http://www.dealersofdeath.com/images/divider.gif" width="380" height="36"></p><br><br>
    
      <DT><font color="#00FF00" size="3"><b>Verant Troubles at Login</b></font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><br>Posted on 5/31/01 03:27 PM by </font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><b>Vnayilu</b></font>
      <DD><font color="#FFFFCC"
size="2"><b><i>Absor posted this to the developers forum for anyone who has been having trouble logging in since the last patch: <br><br>It seems that there is a file that isn't being installed at the moment when you patch to the Live servers. If you want to get logged in right now, just patch to the Test Server (run testeverquest.exe) and cancel once the patch has run. Then you'll be able to log in on the Live servers. We're working to fix the problem, and should have it fixed soon. <br>Sorry for the inconvenience. <br><br>Alan</i></b><br><br></font><br><p align="center"><img src="http://www.dealersofdeath.com/images/divider.gif" width="380" height="36"></p><br><br>
    
      <DT><font color="#00FF00" size="3"><b>Patch Message</b></font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><br>Posted on 5/31/01 09:50 AM by </font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><b>Vnayilu</b></font>
      <DD><font color="#FFFFCC"
size="2">PATCH MESSAGE, MAY 30, 2001 <br><font color=green>Fan Faire </font color=green><br>The new EverQuest expansion, Shadows of Luclin, will be displayed and demonstrated at the Minneapolis Fan Faire! Don't miss this chance to see the latest and greatest upcoming features in the world of Norrath! <br><br>Registration for the event closes on June 4! Hurry and reserve your spot! Visit http://everquest.station.sony.com/fanfaire/ to register or for more information! <br><br><font color=green>Message about our Guide Program </font color=green><br><br>Hail citizens of Norrath! <br><br>Hear my words, for I bring news of great importance. <br><br>Today I present to you an adventure, perhaps the greatest the Lands of Norrath have ever offered. It is a quest of great proportions, and a journey fraught with danger. Fear not though my friends, for the spiritual rewards of this journey far outweigh any hardship involved. <br><br>As of now, we are once again gathering an adventuring party to protect and serve the lands of Norrath. Scribes are lining up even now so that they may take your application to become a Guide of Norrath. <br><br>We are seeking those strong in character, bright in wit, soft with compassion, and filled with joy. <br><br>If you've ever felt good helping a fellow adventurer retrieve his corpse, or with helping someone when they felt all was lost, then this is truly the adventure for you. Or perhaps you feel your sense of humor could bring smiles to the faces of Norrathian citizens. Maybe your renowned acting skills might be of help. If you are kind, compassionate, and helpful, then look no further for the rewarding journey you've sought. <br><br>If you are accepted, I will not mislead you, the journey will be difficult at times. You can be assured that you will be tried... and hopefully you will be found true. In the end though, the citizens of Norrath will benefit from your thoughtful participation, and the lands of Norrath will continue to become a better place. <br><br>If you feel this is something you must be a part of, then I invite you to point your browser to: http://guideapp.everquest.com <br><br>We ask so little of your time, but the benefits you can bring to Norrath are grand. <br><br>A few things to remember: <br><br>1) You must have an active EverQuest account in good standing.<br>2) You must be 18 years of age, or older.<br>3) Your account cannot be shared with any other individual.<br>4) You will need good communication skills.<br>5) Positive attitudes lead to positive results.<br>6) Ability to participate as a part of team is a must.<br><br>Come one, come all... help us to make the lands of Norrath better than they already are... come be a part of the EverQuest Guide Program! <br><br><font color=green>Important Reminder </font color=green><br><br>Due to some of the things we are going to be doing, there is a small chance that some corpses might disappear during the patch. GMs will have the ability to verify any corpses that are lost. That means that they can help you get them back if you do indeed lose one. It is also important to understand that attempting to scam a GM about  lost corpse could mean banning from EverQuest. <br><br>IT IS IMPORTANT THAT YOU PETITION TO HAVE A MISSING CORPSE PROBLEM ADDRESSED WITHIN 5 DAYS OF THE PATCH! <br><br>We will not be recovering corpses that might be lost after that time. In fact, it would be best for you to petition immediately if you have a problem. Don't wait. If you are worried about a corpse that you were unable to deal with before the patch, then please log in and check on it right away after the patch. <br><br>So please make certain that you have as many of your corpses cleaned up as possible before the next patch. We're not expecting a lot of corpses to disappear, but the fewer lying around, the less chance of them disappearing. <br><br><font color=red>Patch Message </font color=red><br><br><font color=green>Zone Changes</font color=green><br><br>Runnyeye has been changed. Something is up in Goblin land... <br>Spell and Song Changes and Bug Fixes <br><br>We've been fixing holes in the spell stacking code. For the most part the changes fix bugs that allowed tricks to get spells to stack that were never intended to stack. <br>Increased duration on Bard Charm songs to 18 seconds from 12 seconds. <br>Fixed the Spell Scroll for Imbue Amber so that Erudite Clerics of Cazic Thule can scribe it. <br>The casting messages for Necromancer pet summoning spells have been changed to be more appropriate. <br>Features and Interface Changes <br><br>The variable %t will now work with /assist. So you can use /assist %t if you wish. Though it should have exactly the same effect as /assist without the %t. <br>%r returns "corpse" for corpses and "NPC" for targeted NPCs. <br>Sense traps failure message text color has been changed to user color 15 (same as other skill messages). The success message was already set to user color 15. <br>Ignore Lists now work the same way that the Friends List does. It has been expanded to 30 names per character per server. The new ignore list is stored in the same ini file as the friends list ( _<#>.ini). The first time a character is created or loaded after the patch their new ignore list will be a copy of the old ignore list, but will from then on be unique to the character. <br>The Alt key now works in several new situations. It will now show item names when in the trade window. Because the trade items of the local player and the trading partner are so close together, the item names of the trading partner will always show up unless the player positions their mouse pointer over the local player part of the trade window, which will cause the game to only show the local player's trade item names. <br>The Alt key will show item names for items in your bank. <br>The Alt key will also pop up names for merchant items and corpse items when you hold it down in merchant mode or loot mode. <br>The Alt key will even pop up names for items in open containers when held down and the mouse cursor is over the open container window (they don't show up otherwise). <br>The client will now automatically reject a /duel request from any player that is on your /ignore list. Some players were using this to annoy players that had ignored them. <br>You also will no longer see /consent messages from people that are on your /ignore list (this was also something people were doing to annoy people that had ignored them). <br>/who GUILD (and the GUILD must be in caps) will now show you the members of your guild in your zone. You can also specify a guild name, such as /who "Irontoe Brigade". <br>/safelock command added. /safelock will lock the EverQuest interface (mostly just mouse clicks, keyboard commands/movement, and most slash commands) with the password that you supply to the command. You must use this command a second time, supplying the same password, to unlock the interface. Passwords are NOT case-sensitive. So to lock your interface, you would type /safelock password. You would do the same to unlock it. REMEMBER: If you forget what password you typed, you will need to reboot your machine. <br><br><font color=red>Item Changes </font color=red><br><br>All the shields in the game that have the Ribcage graphic should now also have the ribcage icon when they are in your inventory. <br>Tinkered Watchman helm should show up now. <br>Ring of Pureblood is now equipable only on your fingers instead of your waist. <br>Grand Master's Leg Wraps and Fists of the Grand Master are now No-Drop. They were intended to be No-Drop when they were created. <br>Peacekeeper Staff and the Bug Collection box are no longer equipable. There are problems that can arise when containers can be equipped, so we had to disable that for these items. <br>Sewing Kits: No existing sewing kits are being changed with this patch. But from now on, kits sold on vendors will be somewhat different. Large Sewing Kits will have 8 slots. Deluxe Sewing Kits will have 10 slots and weight slightly more than the Large Sewing Kit. <br>Changed the color of the Kael SK quest armor from a very pretty blue-green to a more appropriate reddish-gray. <br>Other Stuff <br><br>Changed the spelling of Troubador to Troubadour for the 55th level bard title. <br>King Tormax's spawn rate has been adjusted to be more in line with that of his counterparts in Velious. This is not the sort of thing that we will usually announce, as spawn times and things of that nature are part of the dynamic content of EverQuest. We're announcing this, however, to help avoid some confusion. <br><br>- The EverQuest Team<br> <br><br><br></font><br><p align="center"><img src="http://www.dealersofdeath.com/images/divider.gif" width="380" height="36"></p><br><br>
    
      <DT><font color="#00FF00" size="3"><b>Patch info.</b></font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><br>Posted on 5/29/01 09:24 AM by </font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><b>Vnayilu</b></font>
      <DD><font color="#FFFFCC"
size="2">Patch window being extended on May 30th. Wednesday, May 23 2001 18:32 PST <br><br>The Scheduled patch on May 30th will be starting at 1AM PDT (8AM GMT). The estimated downtime is 13 hours. <br><br>- The EverQuest Operations Team <br><br><br></font><br><p align="center"><img src="http://www.dealersofdeath.com/images/divider.gif" width="380" height="36"></p><br><br>
    
      <DT><font color="#00FF00" size="3"><b>ToV wrap up</b></font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><br>Posted on 5/28/01 12:55 PM by </font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><b>Tuene</b></font>
      <DD><font color="#FFFFCC"
size="2">Last day spent in ToV, short news update as it was completely straight forward besides having more chain boots than we know what to do with... items of significance being yet another Chain BP and Leather legs.  I'll leave it as an exercise to the reader to determine which classes  everyone's alt is going to be from now on :).  List of stuff for the final day only:<br><br>Plate Arms: Scor<br>Plate Boots: Tarkas<br>Plate Gloves: Elesa<br>Plate Gloves: Corazon<br><br>Chain Hat: Sallapus<br>Chain BP: Boann<br>Chain Boots: blank <br>Chain Gloves: Megatryphe<br>Chain Gloves: Boann<br>Chain Boots: blank <br>Chain Boots: blank<br>Chain Bracer: Zerion<br><br>Leather Hat: Amlurial<br>Leather Bracer: Kerasi<br>Leather Bracer: Tuene<br>Leather Hat: Myrick<br>Leather Legs: Haawk<br><br>Silk Gloves: Senadrea<br>Silk Hat: Dameon<br>Silk Arms: Dameon<br>Silk Boots: Sashinal<br>Silk Gloves: Fargius<br><br>Tuene<br><br><br></font><br><p align="center"><img src="http://www.dealersofdeath.com/images/divider.gif" width="380" height="36"></p><br><br>
    
      <DT><font color="#00FF00" size="3"><b>ToV fun and farming</b></font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><br>Posted on 5/27/01 03:06 AM by </font>
      <font color="#FF0000" size="1"><b>Tuene</b></font>
      <DD><font color="#FFFFCC"
size="2"><br>Two more days of fun in the Temple of Veeshan, chasing down teleporting wurms which run a 200m dash faster than Michael Johnson being the highlight of the festivities.  The only other thing remotely approaching this speed is the quickness of Winn in rapidly becoming the first in the guild to have a complete set of KD quest armor (Congrats and thank you for taking care of the incessant CoTH's).  While the drop rate was somewhat disappointing, there were a few extremely nice items, including 2 Chain BP's, another Silk robe (go figure), Plate, Chain and Silk Legs, and a variety of hats to go along with the standard Gloves, Bracers, and Bewties we typically get.<br><br>Without further ado, here's the goodies and their lucky recipients:<br><br>Warriors:<br>Tarkas<br>Rinrek - Boots<br>Scor<br>Malaak - Boots<br>Elesa<br>Conandar - Arms<br>Abira - Legs<br>Mcbain - Bracer<br>Halaria<br><br>Shadowknights:<br>Malagen<br>Karde - Gloves<br>Chold<br><br>Paladins:<br>Xanithor - Arms<br>Relm<br><br>Bards:<br>Corazon<br>Anthem<br><br>Clerics:<br>Shalian<br>Astur<br>Qyen<br>Hark<br>Uberon<br>Tura<br>Aanar<br>Destructor<br>Luth... (no prayer of getting his full name right)<br><br>Shaman:<br>Boann - Bracer<br>Kalourde<br>Thrudd - Legs<br><br>Ranger:<br>Megatryphe - Hat<br>Zerion - Boots<br>Daeeron - Gloves, Boots<br><br>Rogue:<br>Banton - BP, Boots<br>Dratn - BP<br>Sallapus - Arms<br><br>Druids:<br>Tuene - Gloves, Hat<br>Kerasi - Gloves, Hat<br>Amlurial - Bracer, Boots<br>Myrick - Boots<br>Haawk - Hat, Boots<br><br>Monks:<br>Ceyennus - Arms<br>Winja<br>Ceneorn - Bracer<br><br>Wizard:<br>Greymar - Gloves        <br>Senadrea<br>Quinntum - Bracer <br><br>Mage:<br>Winn - Gloves, Boots, Hat<br><br>Enchanter:<br>Sashinal - Robe, Arms <br>Slaine - Legs<br>Fargius - Legs, Boots<br><br>Necro:<br>Dameon<br>Evilosi<br><br><br>Thanks to all for attending so far, more amusement including sacrificial druids (thanks Snare resists) and the almighty dorf FD's (welcome to the prestigeous club Harkaelian) to come tomorrow.<br><br>Tuene<br><br><br><br></font><br><p align="center"><img src="http://www.dealersofdeath.com/images/divider.gif" width="380" height="36"></p><br><br>
